file caravan/ladder_checks.rye the harness gains provision_notes over a comptime rung, the largest body it has taken and the first that reaches a rung's own wire end to end
file caravan/abate.rye one of twenty-four rungs folded to a three-line delegate
file caravan/abandon.rye seat_note widened with its whole family, so no later fold inherits a split
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish carry, bodies, copies, families and the queue's two leaders repinned; the close line corrected to say this fold lifted the leader
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_carry_scan.sh ceiling 121700 -> 119700, the fold history extended, and the absentee-set reading written into the scan's own comments
file caravan/README.md fold W's section, the thirteen-depth fossil-record table, and the arithmetic that closes with no remainder
file crux/REMEMBER.md live edge and Now refreshed to fold W, fold V condensed into the prior-edges line
recommend keep-going The queue's new leader is release_the_standing at 1633 across 24 rungs, with stand_the_mark at 1624 across 29 and reap_oldest at 1584 across 37 behind it. reap_oldest is the better crux on rung count and is one of the four spine bodies fold M already widened, so it may be another free fold; stand_the_mark spans the most rungs of the three leaders. Hash the family first, hash each private symbol's own family before widening it so no successor inherits a split, and read a large absentee set for its SHAPE rather than its count -- thirteen depths told this lap's whole history at a glance where a count would have said only twenty-three. The one gate worth Keaton's eye stays small and unchanged: jinja2 and ply on the pier's Python environment open the seL4 generated headers in a single step, which is an environment change and so his word.
